Z||000000||Steven||06-17-2001||10:39 AM||||I posted a question on the tech side, but thought that after getting no response, maybe the person/people how have the answer don't read the tech side of this forum. Wo I will try again here. I just got a wolf bra for my 85 GT, and I am not sure how to attach it aorund the wheel well area. Could you please help me? TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||CoolBlue87GT||06-17-2001||11:10 AM||||       <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steven:<BR><B>I just got a wolf bra for my 85 GT, and I am not sure how to attach it aorund the wheel well area. Could you please help me? TIA</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The one I have, the bottom part with the covered metal tabs get tucked up under the black spoiler,<BR>and the bungie w/clips gets hooked to a hole that is 1 in long by half inch wide located on the frame.<P>If you look w/ flashlight, you will see the hole. <P>I've got the instruction sheet, will e-mail it to you.<P>I let mine sit in the sun first, it streches better that way.  The first time, it took <BR>two of us to get it lined up and tabs set just right. <P>Once set, on & off is quick.  Make sure the bumber is clean & back of bra is clean.<BR> Would hate to hear of any damage done.<P>Dave<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Del3more.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/del1more.jpg">    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/del2more.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||6
